{
    "background_story": "Rosalee was a renowned botanist who spent most of her life studying the unique properties of the Coumarouna tree, native to the Amazon rainforest. Her fascination with the tree's distinctive fragrance and medicinal properties led her to dedicate her career to unlocking its secrets. Rosalee's tireless efforts took her deep into the jungle, where she worked closely with indigenous communities to learn about their traditional uses of the tree. Her groundbreaking research led to the development of new medicines and sustainable harvesting practices, earning her international recognition and accolades. Rosalee's passion for the Coumarouna tree and its preservation inspired a new generation of scientists and conservationists, cementing her legacy as a champion of rainforest conservation.",
